offer.body=I mend what breaks and make what is missing. A work hall with a supply loft and a little shopfront would suit me. Your Apprentices can learn to make repair kits and equipment for the rest of town.
accepted.body=Here is the workshop plan. Keep a clear aisle between the benches and the door for deliveries.
cancel=I need to put this project aside.
building.body=I will keep my things packed until the artisan workshop is ready. The plot plan lists the materials we need.
cancelled.body=All right. Find me when you are ready to begin again.
back=Understood.
welcome.body=The benches are ready. Ask about workplace upgrades to unlock Crafting, mark a site with your Building Staff and enable Crafting for your Apprentices in the town journal.
how.body=Crafting workplaces use an ordinary workbench. Choose a task, check its skill and bench requirements, and keep the ingredients in town storage. Couriers deliver them and an Apprentice works at the bench. Finished supplies go to Crafted Goods in the warehouse. More workplaces let more people work at once.
gift.confirm=You brought something for me? Let me see.
gift_love=What a thoughtful gift. I have just the place for this.
gift_like=Oh, this will be useful. Thank you.
gift_neutral=Thank you for thinking of me.
gift_dislike=I appreciate the thought, though this is not quite my sort of thing.
